[gd_scene load_steps=6 format=3]

; ROCKET PODS — the Picket's launcher. Six tubes, rippled, indirect.
;
; NO NEW SCRIPT. This is the FIFTH set of exports on
; ai_weapon_grenade_launcher.gd, after the mortar, the grenade launcher, the
; turret grenade launcher and the cluster launcher. FRAME_ANATOMY.md section
; 3.4's rule — "you need a subclass if and only if the round is not a hitscan
; ray, and a .tres plus ai_weapon_grenade_launcher.gd is enough for anything
; that lobs a charge" — answers this weapon for free: lob_speed solves the arc
; from the ground onto the target, impact_fused bursts the round where it
; lands, and nothing about a rocket pod needs a sixth behaviour.
;
; THE ROUND IS THE MORTAR'S. ai_mortar_round.tscn is a RigidBody3D with
; blast_damage, fuse_time, explode_on_bounce and flight_time — every property
; the launcher overrides on release — and it whistles down on the last second
; of its arc, which is the one audible warning an arcing round can give the
; thing it is about to land on. A second projectile scene would be the same
; object with a different silhouette at 80 m in the air.
;
; HIGH ARC, DELIBERATELY. The pack is canted 54 degrees on PodCant
; (picket.tscn:423) and walker.gd:224 adds elevation on top, so the launcher's
; real band is 42 to 89 degrees and it CANNOT point at the ground. That is the
; approved silhouette, so the ballistics have to agree with it: high_arc fires
; the steep root of the same equation, and a round leaving a 70-degree tube on
; a 17-degree trajectory would be the frame lying about itself.
;
; lob_speed 32 IS NEAR THE LIMIT, ON PURPOSE. Flat-ground reach at this speed
; is v*v/g = 104 m, and max_effective_range is 95 — so the gun is working at
; its own ballistic edge at full range, which is where a 95 m reach stops being
; a number on a card. It also pins time of flight: on the high arc that is
; roughly 2*lob_speed/g, i.e. 5.5 s at 95 m and 6.2 s at 60. A round that is
; airborne for six seconds lands where its target WAS, which is why targeting
; is PATIENT (pick something that will still be there) and why this weapon is
; not an answer to a moving aircraft. See docs/integration/PICKET.md's
; amendment: that is an open identity question, not a bug in this file.
;
; min_effective_range 18 IS A SAFETY NUMBER, not flavour, and it overrides the
; brief's 0.0 — which was written for a hitscan burst. On the high arc a round
; fired at something ten metres away goes almost straight up and comes almost
; straight back down, and ai-wep_cluster.tscn already carries the comment
; explaining what that does to the frame that fired it. The Picket's CLAWS
; built-in is what it has below eighteen metres.

